  <h2>1. About DB Diff</h2>
  <p>
    DB Diff is a command-line tool that compares the rows of one table across two databases. It is provided by Club
    Matto in two tiers: a free, open-source CLI and a Pro tier.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Free tier</h2>
  <p>
    The free tier of DB Diff is available under the terms of its
    <a href="https://github.com/clubmatto/vetrina/blob/main/db-diff/LICENSE">open-source license</a>. You may use it
    without charge for any purpose, subject to that license. No account, registration, or payment is required.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Pro tier</h2>
  <p>
    The Pro tier adds cross engine comparison: a table can be compared between two different engines, because each value
    is reduced to a canonical form before it is hashed. Pro is planned as a paid subscription service.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pro is in early access.</strong> While we build licensing, we provide Pro builds free of charge on request.
    No key, account, or payment is required, and the tool does not transmit your data or your schema to us. The prices
    on the <a href="/products/db-diff/">product page</a> apply when licensing becomes available, and we will tell you
    before that changes for a build you already have.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once Pro is generally available, subscribing means paying the fees listed on the product page at the time of
    purchase. Fees may be monthly or annual and are billed in advance. All fees are non-refundable except where required
    by law. You may cancel at any time, and cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. No
    partial refunds are provided.
  </p>

